Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Cloud Contacts: LinkedIn/Instagram social import via the
 stock vCard pipeline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

'Import contacts' (Settings) and shared/opened files now also accept:
- LinkedIn Connections.csv (Data privacy -> Get a copy of your data)
- Instagram followers_1.json / following.json (Download your information)

SocialImporter content-sniffs the picked file (the picker's temp copy is
always renamed *.vcf, so extensions are meaningless), converts social rows
to a temporary vCard 3.0 file, and hands it to the unchanged
ImportContactsDialog/VcfImporter pipeline — the user still picks the target
source (phone storage or a synced account such as Gmail). Profile URLs land
as website entries, so the contact detail view renders tappable links that
app-link into the installed LinkedIn/Instagram app. Real vCards and
unrecognized files pass through untouched.

The GET_CONTENT picker widens from text/x-vcard to a vcard/csv/json
EXTRA_MIME_TYPES set. Verified by a JVM harness driving
SocialImporter.maybeConvertToVcf over sample exports (2 LinkedIn rows with
quoted commas + preamble, both Instagram shapes, vCard/garbage passthrough).
